Fix the working directory on Windows

Two defects, one of which stops the library linking at all.

1. PR #578 does not link against 2.4.0.

The PR was written against 2.3.0-era master, where Session::run() set the
child's directory with Pty::setWorkingDirectory(). Between 2.3.0 and 2.4.0
upstream introduced Pty::setInitialWorkingDirectory() -- which normalises a
trailing slash, forwards to setWorkingDirectory() and fixes up PWD -- and moved
both call sites in Session::run() onto it. The PR only provides
setWorkingDirectory() in its Windows branch, so:

    Session.cpp:(.text+0x688f): undefined reference to
        `Konsole::Pty::setInitialWorkingDirectory(QString const&)'

The PR still reports as mergeable on GitHub because the conflict is semantic,
not textual -- nothing it touches overlaps the lines that changed. Worth knowing
before trusting "mergeable: clean" on a PR this old.

The Windows branch gets its own setInitialWorkingDirectory() mirroring the Unix
one, minus the PWD handling: that exists so a POSIX shell inherits a symlinked
path unresolved, and neither ConPTY nor the environment block (see below) can
carry it today.

2. The working directory was dropped on the floor regardless.

Pty::setWorkingDirectory() was an empty stub, and ConPtyProcess::startProcess()
took a workingDir parameter it never used -- the CreateProcessW call passes NULL
with the real argument sitting next to it, commented out, from the original
ptyqt sources. So QTermWidget::setWorkingDirectory() silently did nothing and
every terminal opened wherever the host application happened to be. gcc catches
both halves as -Wunused-parameter, which is how this was noticed.

Now the stub stores the value, Pty::start() falls back to it when the caller
passes nothing, and CreateProcessW receives it -- through toNativeSeparators(),
since Qt hands out '/' and this argument reaches the Win32 API unmodified, and
as NULL rather than an empty string, which is how CreateProcessW spells "inherit
the parent's".

STILL OUTSTANDING, deliberately not fixed here: the environment block is dropped
in exactly the same way. envArg is built and then passed as NULL two lines above
the working directory, so TERM and everything Session adds never reach the child.
That has to be fixed before an MSYS2 shell can be launched properly -- MSYSTEM
and CHERE_INVOKING are passed the same way -- but it is a larger change than a
one-argument fix and belongs in its own patch.

Upstream: not submitted; belongs on PR #578, which is not being merged --
         see 0001's header
Applies-to: all environments (the changed code is behind Q_OS_WIN)

--- a/lib/Pty.h
+++ b/lib/Pty.h
@@ -281,6 +281,7 @@
     bool _utf8;
 #ifdef Q_OS_WIN
     std::unique_ptr<IPtyProcess> m_proc;
+    QString _workingDir;
 #endif
 };
 
--- a/lib/Pty.cpp
+++ b/lib/Pty.cpp
@@ -463,8 +463,22 @@
     return _eraseChar;
 }
 
-void Pty::setWorkingDirectory(const QString & /*dir*/)
+void Pty::setWorkingDirectory(const QString &dir)
 {
+    _workingDir = dir;
+}
+
+void Pty::setInitialWorkingDirectory(const QString &dir)
+{
+    QString pwd = dir;
+
+    // remove trailing slash in the path when appropriate
+    // example: /usr/share/icons/ ==> /usr/share/icons
+    if (pwd.length() > 1 && pwd.endsWith(QLatin1Char('/'))) {
+        pwd.chop(1);
+    }
+
+    setWorkingDirectory(pwd);
 }
 
